The synonym "aminoadipic acid" is related but not identical to "2-aminoadipic acid." The label specifies the position of the amino group (at position 2), which is a crucial detail for chemical identification and differentiation from other aminoadipic acids. While "aminoadipic acid" is broader and could refer to any aminoadipic acid, "2-aminoadipic acid" is specific to the isomer with the amino group at position 2. Therefore, they are not interchangeable in a precise biomedical context.
