Comment: "Sadness, per se, is a basic emotion with negative valence and low arousal. Sadness has significant evolutionary implications from behavioral, cognitive, social and health perspectives. As sadness persists, physical and cognitive symptoms including fatigue, difficulty concentrating, disrupted sleep, and loss of interest or pleasure in activities may become present, when dominant, interfere with personal, social, or occupational functioning. This state is distinct from normative sadness or grief and should be differentiated from the syndromic presentation of Major Depressive Disorder."
