The synonym "Long finger bone" is related but not exact to "Long phalanx of finger." While both terms refer to elongated structures in the finger, "finger bone" is a broader term that can include other bones in the finger such as metacarpals, whereas "phalanx" specifically refers to the bones in the fingers and toes. Therefore, they are not interchangeable in all contexts.
